nightsiege.guide.bonus.body:
Between sieges something good happens now and then.

## Aurora
@minecraft:glow_ink_sac|In about one quiet night in eight (no siege due) an aurora dances in the sky. Within 64 blocks of a core it slowly heals you and grants 1 experience point every 3 minutes.

nightsiege.guide.events.body:
From level 3 a siege brings an event 45 % of the time. It is never announced: you see it in the sky and on the monsters. During an event zombies, skeletons, creepers and spiders take on its look. The blood moon brings the blood-cursed: pale zombies in bloody rags and hoods, skeletons in torn cloaks, all with glowing red eyes.

@minecraft:redstone_block|§cBlood moon§r: red moon and sky, 1.5× as many monsters, tougher and harder hitting.
@minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull|§4Boss night§r (every 4th night up to night 36, no event): at its end a boss comes – Grave King, Spider Queen, Bone Lich, Illager Warlord, Frost Jarl (a stomp through the shield, walls of ice, an avalanche), Ember Colossus (cracks of lava, breaks in two at half health), Storm Witch (flies, chain lightning, a storm sweeps the walls, lands every 30 s) or Ram Titan (runs through gate and wall, leaves craters). What they break comes back after the night. The night is only won when it falls; then everyone gets a crate as from a fragment night. A lost boss night brings the same boss again the night after.
@minecraft:gold_block|§6Night of Four§r (nights 20 and 40): no waves, no clock – the four bosses of the boss nights before come back, two at a time with about half their health each; the next two 20 s after the first two fell, at the latest after 3 minutes. When all have fallen every defender gets the Crown of the Siege (wearable), a crown stands on the core and there is a fragment crate. A lost Night of Four comes again the night after.
@minecraft:netherite_sword|§4Double boss night§r (every 2nd night from night 41): 5 minutes of normal waves, then two bosses at once (about three quarters of their health each) with a last big wave. When both fall the night is won; if they still stand at dawn it is lost.
@minecraft:zombie_head|§eTheme wave§r: the whole night is a single kind of monster.
@minecraft:black_concrete|§5Solar eclipse§r: once the countdown is done, the sun goes dark at noon and the siege comes by day. The undead do not burn and phantoms join in. A horn warns shortly before.
@minecraft:cobweb|§7Fog night§r: you see only a few blocks, the monsters are silent, more spiders and creepers.
@minecraft:lightning_rod|§bThunder night§r: lightning strikes the attackers and charges creepers. Tesla coils hit 50 % harder. No natural lightning, nothing catches fire.
@minecraft:crying_obsidian|§4Nether rift§r: rifts open around the base and half the attackers come from the Nether. Ash falls from the sky.
@minecraft:powder_snow_bucket|§fFrost night§r: a blizzard, strays instead of skeletons. Anyone out in the open slows down and freezes (no damage). Leather armour keeps the cold out.

Events never change blocks. Like the blood moon, frost, rift and fog nights have a moon of their own.

## With shaders
On start Night Siege puts a shader pack of its own into the shaderpacks folder: §6NightSiege-Photon§r (a changed Photon by SixthSurge). Pick it in the Iris shader menu. It draws every event itself: real fog, red sky and event moon, the eclipse with its corona, and the aurora.
Other shader packs keep their own sky. There the events show through mist wisps, snow, ash, lightning and the monster looks; the eclipse darkens the day.

nightsiege.guide.perks.body:
Every beaten dungeon gives a night fragment. Set it into your siege core: fragment in hand, right-click the core. The next siege then becomes a §dspecial night§r with the fragment's event.

- 30 % more monsters
- double experience
- a chest of loot next to the core if you hold
- Only one fragment at a time sits in the core

@nightsiege:night_fragment_blood|§cBlood Fragment§r → Blood Moon (Stone Crypt, Desert Crypt)
@nightsiege:night_fragment_mist|§7Mist Fragment§r → Fog Night (Poison Swamp)
@nightsiege:night_fragment_frost|§bFrost Fragment§r → Frost Night (Frost Keep)
@nightsiege:night_fragment_storm|§9Storm Fragment§r → Thunder Night (Illager Keep)
@nightsiege:night_fragment_shadow|§6Shadow Fragment§r → Eclipse (Deep Dungeon); comes by day
@nightsiege:night_fragment_ember|§6Ember Fragment§r → Nether Rift (Nether Forge, Basalt Forge)

Old core fragments from the first dungeons no longer work.

nightsiege.guide.traps.body:
Anyone can craft traps; only an engineer with the matching skill can set them. They only hit monsters, never players - by day as well. Every trap grows with its owner's tier.

## Cap per player
How many floor traps of one kind you may have at once rises with the tier. Towers have a fixed cap. The exact numbers are in the skill window.

@nightsiege:spike_trap|Spike Trap: damage + slow. Recipe: 3 iron over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:snare_trap|Snare Trap: holds everything around. 3 string, string-iron-string, 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:mortar_tower|Mortar Tower: shells in an arc onto a target spot (Ability 2), over walls too, no block damage. Iron-gunpowder-iron, iron-TNT-iron, 3 cobblestone
@nightsiege:arrow_turret|Arrow Turret: shoots monsters, endless arrows. Iron-dispenser-iron, iron-bow-iron, 3 cobblestone
@nightsiege:flame_trap|Flame Trap: sets alight. Iron, fire charge, iron over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:potion_tower|Potion Thrower: throws poison potions onto groups. Glass-fermented eye-glass, iron-brewing stand-iron, 3 cobblestone
@nightsiege:tesla_coil|Tesla Coil: chain lightning, no ammunition, charges slowly. Copper, lightning rod, copper / iron, redstone block, iron / 3 cobblestone

nightsiege.guide.abilities.body:
While you wear the kit, the §ekit bar§r at the bottom shows everything at a glance: your class crest on the left, then your abilities, health, armour (under water: air) and hunger in the middle, and the hotbar on the right in two rows (1–5 on top, 6–9 and the off hand below). Each slot shows its key small in its lower right corner.

- §eBig slots§r: Q (ult), F (Ability 2), X (second ult)
- §eMiddle arch on top§r: the gain keys N, M (and J) with your crate gains as small symbols, like the effects on the right and the companions on the left
- §eSmall slots below§r: your spells, heals, the storm step (warriors, R) and one slot each for arrows and potions; for these two hold the key and turn the mouse wheel to change, a tap throws the potion or goes back to normal arrows
- Only what you have learned gets a slot; without abilities the bar gets narrower
- The dark fill and the number show the cooldown; grey means: outside the night; a ready ult has a gold frame
- A gold frame around the arrow slot: a special arrow kind is picked
- Without the kit you see the normal Minecraft hotbar
- Every key can be changed under Options → Controls → Night Siege

## Q – ult (the symbol of the ult talent in your skill tree)
@minecraft:blaze_rod|Arrow Storm (bow): for a while every shot fires several extra arrows.
@minecraft:dragon_breath|Power Shot (bow): your next shot deals many times the damage.
@minecraft:compass|Hunt (bow or crossbow): marks every monster around, they take more damage from everyone.
@minecraft:firework_rocket|Bolt Volley (crossbow): you fire a volley of bolts.
@minecraft:cobweb|Net Rain (crossbow): nets fall on every monster around, they are stuck and take damage.
@minecraft:diamond_sword|Execute (blade): kills the monster in view at once when it is low – bosses too.
@minecraft:breeze_rod|Whirlwind (blade): damage to everything around you, it flies away.
@minecraft:heavy_core|Ground Slam (might): damage around, the hit fly up and are slowed hard.
@minecraft:beacon|Holy Light (might): damage around, the undead burn, teammates are healed.
@minecraft:redstone_block|Overcharge (mechanics): your arrow turrets and tesla coils fire much faster for a while.
@minecraft:trident|Thunderstorm (mechanics): a chain lightning from your hand jumps from monster to monster.
@minecraft:tnt_minecart|Bombardment (chemistry): explosions hit the nearest monsters.
@minecraft:lingering_potion|Toxic Cloud (chemistry): poisons, weakens and slows every monster around you.
@minecraft:echo_shard|Wild Hunt (wild): invulnerable ghost wolves hunt for you for a while.
@minecraft:iron_block|Titan (wild): a giant golem fights for you for a while and slams the ground.
@minecraft:skeleton_skull|Army of the Dead (dead): monsters that fell lately rise and fight for you.
@minecraft:sculk_catalyst|Soul Storm (dead): every soul at once as a ghost wave, damage per soul.
@minecraft:iron_horse_armor|Shield Charge (shield): you charge forward, damage, knockback and slowness.
@minecraft:goat_horn|Taunt (shield): every monster around attacks you, you get resistance, everyone absorption.
@minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple|Mass Heal (blessing): heals every player around and gives regeneration.
@minecraft:end_crystal|Holy Sanctuary (blessing): players in the circle take far less damage, monsters stay out.

## F – Ability 2
@nightsiege:remote_control|Engineer, remote in hand: on an own trap it overcharges, on a monster it marks, on a block it aims the mortars. The alchemist throws his potion zone with it.
@minecraft:lead|Summoner (not the soul catcher), staff in hand: every companion attacks the monster in view or holds the block in view.
@minecraft:glistering_melon_slice|Medic and warden: casts the heal used last on the teammate in view, otherwise on you.

## X – second ult (a crate reward, 90 s pause)
@minecraft:clock|Battle Trance (warrior): monsters around much slower for 5 s, you faster.
@minecraft:target|Lure Arrow (archer): monsters around the impact walk only there for 5 s.
@minecraft:amethyst_shard|Mirror Shield (guardian): for 5 s arrows and fireballs bounce back to the shooter.
@minecraft:lodestone|Magnetic Field (engineer): pulls monsters around to the spot you look at for 3 s.
@minecraft:chorus_fruit|Soul Swap (summoner): swap places with the companion in view, without one with the monster in view (no bosses).

## R, G, Y, C, V, B – your picks
The key works at once. Spells cost souls, the costs are in the skill tree.
@minecraft:zombie_head|Raise Corpse (necromancer): the next corpse rises for a short while, fights for you and bursts at the end.
@minecraft:bone_block|Bone Wall (necromancer): a wall of bones in front of you.
@minecraft:wither_rose|Curse Zone (necromancer): a circle around the target; monsters inside take more damage, are slower and lose health.
@minecraft:soul_lantern|Ghost Swarm (soul catcher): ghosts fly at your target and its neighbours, 6 s pause.
@minecraft:ghast_tear|Fright (soul catcher): monsters around the target flee and attack no one.
@minecraft:goat_horn|Call (beast tamer, golemsmith): your wolves or your golem come back to you.
@minecraft:honey_bottle|Healing Hand (medic): heals the teammate in view, without one yourself (half as much).
@minecraft:amethyst_shard|Ward Shield (warden): the barrier goes at once to the teammate in view.
@minecraft:glass|Protective Dome (blessing): a dome around you, monsters are pushed out, missiles fall apart.
@minecraft:lingering_potion|Potion zones (alchemist), the colour of the flask shows the potion: red healing, pink regeneration, yellow strength, turquoise swiftness (for players) – green poison, light blue slowness, grey weakness (against monsters).
@minecraft:bundle|Arrow kinds (every archer has the quiver): normal arrows and every kind with shots in the quiver get a key; the one in use has the gold frame.
